crates/ddai-libm: glibc 2.39 math functions
------------------------------------------------------------------------

`crates/ddai-libm` re-implements, in Rust, the math functions of the GNU C
Library 2.39 (Ubuntu 24.04, x86-64 FMA variant) that DDNet 20.1's physics
calls on Linux, so that Linux and Windows compute identical bits (decisions
D-047, D-127). The source of each file is stated in its header; the tables in
`crates/ddai-libm/src/tables.rs` are generated from the glibc sources by
`tools/libm-tables/gen_tables.py`. No file was copied from a non-GPL-compatible
source. The parts and their licences:

* `sincosf.rs` (`sinf`, `cosf`), `powf.rs`, `log.rs`, `pow.rs`: the algorithms
  of ARM Limited's optimized-routines (https://github.com/ARM-software/
  optimized-routines, `math/sincosf.c`, `powf.c`, `log.c`, `pow.c` and their
  data files, the revision of 2018 that glibc 2.28 imported), licensed MIT
  (the upstream project is today "MIT OR Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception"; the
  MIT alternative is used). Each of the four files carries the MIT text:

